# SEO Audit Console — environment variables
# Configure these in your MCP client (e.g. claude_desktop_config.json "env"), or export them
# when running the local scripts. Only GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS is required.
#
# Optional API keys: leave blank to disable. A value that is still a placeholder ("your-key-here",
# "<your key>", "changeme", "xxx", anything with "example", or an unsubstituted ${...}) is treated
# as unset too, with one stderr line saying so - the tier stays off instead of failing with 401s.

# Path to a Google Cloud service-account JSON key with Search Console API access.
# (Add the service account's email as a user on each GSC property you want to audit.)
GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS=/absolute/path/to/service-account.json

# Where per-property SQLite databases + exported reports are stored. If unset, the folder saved
# by the data_location tool (~/.seo-audit-console.json) is used, else ~/Documents/seo-audit-console.
SAC_DATA_DIR=/absolute/path/to/seo-audit-console-data

# SEOCoral fork: DataForSEO and Majestic were removed (paid). Keyword data comes from Google Ads below.

# Optional — Chrome UX Report (CrUX) API key: real-user Core Web Vitals (LCP, INP, CLS) for the
# origin and your top pages, via sync_crux / refresh_property. Free: a Google Cloud API key with the
# Chrome UX Report API enabled (quota 150 queries/min). Leave blank to disable.
CRUX_API_KEY=

# Optional/advanced — pin the local passage-scoring model to a device: dml (DirectX 12 GPU on
# Windows) or cpu. Unset, it tries the GPU and falls back to CPU by itself. Also used by
# find_duplicates' embedding model.
SAC_RERANK_DEVICE=

# Optional/advanced — the local browser dashboard. It starts by itself after a refresh, sync,
# crawl, inspection or audit; SAC_AUTOSERVE=0 stops that (open_dashboard still starts it).
SAC_AUTOSERVE=
# Bind address (default 127.0.0.1; 0.0.0.0 in a container so a published port reaches it - it
# still answers only requests addressed to localhost), a fixed port (default: random), and the
# host written into the links it hands out (default 127.0.0.1).
SAC_DASHBOARD_BIND=
SAC_DASHBOARD_PORT=
SAC_DASHBOARD_URL_HOST=

# SEOCoral fork — Google Ads API (Keyword Planner): free search volume + keyword ideas with your MCC.
# Run `node scripts/google-ads-auth.mjs <client_secret.json>` once; it writes this file.
# The developer token needs Basic access (Explorer access cannot use Keyword Planner).
GOOGLE_ADS_CREDENTIALS=/absolute/path/to/credenciales/google-ads.json
# Optional overrides of the file's fields:
# GOOGLE_ADS_CUSTOMER_ID=        # account the planner runs under (a client with spend = exact volumes)
# GOOGLE_ADS_API_VERSION=v26
# GOOGLE_ADS_CACHE_DAYS=30
# SAC_VOLUME_PROVIDER=           # google-ads (default when set) | dataforseo
